## 🏗️ TRANSFORMERS ARCHITECTURE

### Background: Attention Mechanism

**Problem Solved**: RNNs struggle with long sequences, can't parallelize.

**Solution**: Attention allows direct connection between any positions.

**Attention Formula**:
- Query, Key, Value vectors
- Attention weights: softmax(Q · K^T / √d)
- Output: weighted sum of Values
- Captures relationships between all positions

**Self-Attention**:
- Query, Key, Value from same input
- Each position attends to all positions
- Parallel computation
- Captures dependencies

### Transformer Architecture

**Overview**:
- Encoder-decoder structure
- Stack of identical layers
- Each layer has two sub-layers:
  - Multi-head self-attention
  - Feed-forward network

**Encoder**:
- Input embedding + positional encoding
- Multiple attention/feed-forward layers
- Outputs contextualized representations
- Each position sees all other positions

**Decoder**:
- Output embedding + positional encoding
- Masked self-attention (can't attend to future)
- Cross-attention (attends to encoder output)
- Feed-forward network
- Generates output sequentially

**Key Components**:

**Positional Encoding**:
- Encodes position information
- Sine and cosine functions
- Added to embeddings
- Enables position awareness
- Doesn't require explicit position input

**Multi-Head Attention**:
- Multiple attention "heads"
- Each head learns different representation
- Outputs concatenated
- Increases model capacity
- Usually 8-12 heads

**Feed-Forward Network**:
- Two linear layers with activation
- Applied to each position
- Same parameters across positions
- Expansion then reduction

**Layer Normalization**:
- Normalizes inputs to layers
- Stabilizes training
- Usually before sublayers
- Different from batch normalization

**Residual Connections**:
- Shortcut from input to output
- x + Sublayer(x)
- Enables deep networks
- Improves gradient flow

### Variants

**BERT (Bidirectional Encoder Representations)**:
- Encoder-only architecture
- Bidirectional pre-training
- Good for classification tasks
- Can't generate text directly
- Fine-tuned for downstream tasks

**GPT (Generative Pre-trained Transformer)**:
- Decoder-only architecture
- Unidirectional pre-training
- Can generate text
- Language model
- In-context learning capability

**T5 (Text-to-Text Transfer Transformer)**:
- Encoder-decoder architecture
- All tasks as text-to-text
- Unified framework
- Pre-trained on diverse objectives

**RoBERTa, ALBERT, DeBERTa**:
- BERT improvements
- Better pre-training
- More efficient
- Better performance

