#### Q16: How would you monitor and detect model degradation in production?

**Answer:**

**Model Degradation Definition:**
Model performance drops below acceptable threshold due to:
- Data distribution shift (covariate/label shift)
- Model becomes stale
- Training data no longer representative
- Concept drift (patterns change)

**Monitoring Strategy:**

**1. Data Drift Detection**:

**Covariate Shift** (P(X) changes, P(Y|X) same):
```
Example: "young" model trained 95% men, now 50% women
Gender distribution changed
Model may have learned spurious patterns

Detection:
├─ Statistical tests:
│  ├─ Kolmogorov-Smirnov test (continuous)
│  ├─ Chi-square test (categorical)
│  └─ Population Stability Index (PSI)
├─ Monitor feature distributions:
│  ├─ Mean, median, std
│  └─ Quantiles (p25, p75)
└─ Alerting: If deviation > threshold
```

**Label Shift** (P(Y) changes, P(X|Y) same):
```
Example: Fraud ratio changed from 1% to 5%
Prior probability changed
Model predictions biased

Detection:
├─ Monitor label distribution
├─ Compare historical vs current
└─ Check if ratios changed significantly
```

**Concept Drift** (P(Y|X) changes):
```
Example: User preferences for recommendations changed
Same input → different optimal output
Most dangerous type

Detection:
├─ Ground truth labeling
├─ Collect labels for predictions
├─ Compare accuracy to baseline
├─ More difficult, requires label availability
```

**2. Model Performance Monitoring**:

**For Classification**:
```
Metrics to track:
├─ Accuracy (overall)
├─ Precision, Recall per class
├─ F1-score
├─ AUC-ROC
├─ Confusion matrix

Baselines:
├─ Training metric (what we expect)
├─ Baseline model (simple comparison)
├─ Previous week/month (trend)

Alerting thresholds:
├─ If metric drops > 5%: Warning
├─ If metric drops > 10%: Critical alert
├─ If consistent degradation: Trigger retrain
```

**For Regression**:
```
Metrics:
├─ MAE: Average absolute error
├─ RMSE: Root mean squared error
├─ MAPE: Mean absolute percentage error
├─ R²: Variance explained

Track over time:
├─ Per segment (geographic, user type)
├─ Overall and by percentile
└─ Identify which segments degrade
```

