**4. Root Cause Analysis**:

When degradation detected:

```
1. Analyze what changed:
   ├─ Which segments affected? (geography, user type)
   ├─ Which features changed? (data drift analysis)
   ├─ When did it start?
   └─ How severe? (all predictions or subset)

2. Data investigation:
   ├─ Sample recent predictions
   ├─ Compare to historical predictions
   ├─ Check ground truth labels
   ├─ Identify misclassified examples
   └─ Look for patterns

3. Possible causes:
   ├─ Data quality issue (bad labels, missing values)
   ├─ Feature engineering change (pipeline bug)
   ├─ External event (market change, seasonality)
   ├─ Model staleness (distribution drift)
   └─ Code bug (inference logic)
```

**5. Response Actions**:

**Immediate (Emergency)**:
```
If accuracy drops > 15%:
├─ Page on-call engineer
├─ Disable or rollback model
├─ Fallback to previous version
├─ Use rule-based alternative
└─ Notify stakeholders
```

**Short-term (Urgent)**:
```
If accuracy drops 5-15%:
├─ Investigate root cause
├─ Retrain model on recent data
├─ A/B test new version
├─ Adjust decision thresholds
└─ Update feature logic if needed
```

**Long-term (Proactive)**:
```
├─ Implement automatic retraining (weekly/daily)
├─ Add concept drift detection
├─ Improve data quality checks
├─ Diversify training data
├─ Build robust features
└─ Create monitoring alerts for indicators
```

